Bad Hacker wrote ...

>So, generally, I should #twoweapon even if I cannot get it past basic
>skill? I have not put any skill points in saber or longsword, but did
>recently find a silver saber. Also, many more sacrifices have yet to
>yield a weapon from Set.

A Barbarian will prevail either with one good weapon, or two-weaponing.
For a combat wombat, your current AC might be a small problem,
but you can enchant your armor when you find the Wand from
the Castle, at least. Barbarians have good dexterity, so hitting
with basic 2-weaponing skill isn't a problem.

If you really want extra AC, use one (very good) weapon with a Shield of Reflection.
But with a decently enchanted shieldless armour kit you'll have
good enough AC anyway, so you should by all means advance 2-weapon
combat and the appropriate weapon skills (long sword and saber).
And then, observe how your enemies go down quickly!

>How much further can I go down and expect to find priests or altars? 

VoD, below the Castle. It's a rather special unaligned altar, so be very
careful around it. There can be Dungeon -like levels below Medusa,
but I've yet to see altars in them.

>Shops end at the castle level, right?

Yes. There are only abandoned shops in a certain level beyond that point.
A shop isn't really complete without a shopkeeper, I think...

